The hazards that would have broken a naive translation, all verified against the C binary rather than reasoned about:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mscanf[0m skipping whitespace across newlines ([38;5;10m"\n\n\n42"[0m → 42, where a [38;5;10mread_line[0m translation gives 0)[0m[0m
- glibc's two-stage overflow: [38;5;10mstrtol[0m saturates to [38;5;10mLONG_MAX[0m/[38;5;10mLONG_MIN[0m, then the store through [38;5;10mint *[0m truncates. [38;5;10m9223372036854775808[0m → [38;5;10mffffffff…[0m, [38;5;10m-99999999999999999999999[0m → [38;5;10m00000000…[0m, [38;5;10m4294967296[0m → [38;5;10m00000000…[0m. [38;5;10mi32::from_str[0m would fail the first; wrapping accumulation would differ again.[0m[0m
- failed conversion leaving [38;5;10mx[0m at its initializer rather than being zeroed[0m[0m
- NUL and [38;5;10m0xff[0m bytes on stdin (byte-oriented reader, so invalid UTF-8 can't panic or diverge)[0m[0m
- read errors ([38;5;10mEISDIR[0m, [38;5;10m/dev/null[0m) producing the [38;5;10mx=0[0m image, exit 0, empty stderr[0m[0m
- pipe vs. file stdout, where [38;5;10mprintf[0m buffering changes but the bytes must not[0m[0m
- 100,000-byte digit runs[0m[0m
